<title>POLAND: Polish industrial output up 0.7 pct in August.</title>
<headline>Polish industrial output up 0.7 pct in August.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output (unadjusted) rose 0.7 percent in August after a 4.9 percent rise in July, and was 6.9 percent higher than in August 1995, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>Industrial output rose 8.8 percent in the January-August period, against a 11.5 percent rise in the same time last year.  </p>
<p>POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	 AUGUST	JULY	 AUG 95</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	  0.7     4.9  (4.8)     7.0</p>
<p> yr/yr change			  6.9    13.2  13.1)     9.1</p>
<p> index (mthly avg 1994=100)     20.6     N/A (19.2)   *34.4</p>
<p> mining m/m change		  -1.6    13.3 (14.1)     4.0</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change		-8.5    -0.5  (0.2)    10.0</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	  0.7     5.1  (4.9)     7.6</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change	9.3    16.8 (16.5)    10.8</p>
<p> utilities m/m change		3.0    -5.2 (-5.2)    -2.0</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change	   -0.1    -4.9 (-4.8)    -4.5</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>NOTES: Revised data in brackets. July 1996 had 24 working days, August 1996 had 23 working days and August 1995 had 22 working days. (*) 1992=100</p>
